{"translation":{"id":"eng_asv","name":"American Standard Version (1901)","website":"https://ebible.org/Scriptures/details.php?id=eng-asv","licenseUrl":"https://ebible.org/Scriptures/details.php?id=eng-asv","license":{"attribution":"not-required","commercialUse":"allowed","derivatives":"allowed","copyleft":false,"publicDomain":true},"shortName":"ASV","englishName":"American Standard Version (1901)","language":"eng","textDirection":"ltr","sha256":"154967f9f68504bdf9a8d7abaae4ef6a93f20f779df84e62c1c8828427731839","availableFormats":["json"],"listOfBooksApiLink":"/api/eng_asv/books.json","completeTranslationApiLink":"/api/eng_asv/complete.json","simpleCompleteTranslationApiLink":"/api/eng_asv/complete.simple.json","numberOfBooks":66,"totalNumberOfChapters":1189,"totalNumberOfVerses":31102,"languageName":"English","languageEnglishName":"English"},"book":{"id":"TIT","name":"Titus","commonName":"Titus","title":"THE EPISTLE OF PAUL TO TITUS","numberOfChapters":3,"totalNumberOfVerses":46},"chapters":[null,{"numberOfVerses":16,"chapter":{"number":1,"content":[{"type":"verse","number":1,"content":["Paul, a servant of God, and an apostle of Jesus Christ, according to the faith of God’s elect, and the knowledge of the truth which is according to godliness,"]},{"type":"verse","number":2,"content":["in hope of eternal life, which God, who cannot lie, promised before times eternal;"]},{"type":"verse","number":3,"content":["but in his own seasons manifested his word in the message, wherewith I was intrusted according to the commandment of God our Saviour;"]},{"type":"verse","number":4,"content":["to Titus, my true child after a common faith: Grace and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Saviour."]},{"type":"line_break"},{"type":"verse","number":5,"content":["For this cause left I thee in Crete, that thou shouldest set in order the things that were wanting, and appoint elders in every city, as I gave thee charge;"]},{"type":"verse","number":6,"content":["if any man is blameless, the husband of one wife, having children that believe, who are not accused of riot or unruly."]},{"type":"verse","number":7,"content":["For the bishop must be blameless, as God’s steward; not self-willed, not soon angry, no brawler, no striker, not greedy of filthy lucre;"]},{"type":"verse","number":8,"content":["but given to hospitality, a lover of good, sober-minded, just, holy, self-controlled;"]},{"type":"verse","number":9,"content":["holding to the faithful word which is according to the teaching, that he may be able both to exhort in the sound doctrine, and to convict the gainsayers."]},{"type":"verse","number":10,"content":["For there are many unruly men, vain talkers and deceivers, specially they of the circumcision,"]},{"type":"verse","number":11,"content":["whose mouths must be stopped; men who overthrow whole houses, teaching things which they ought not, for filthy lucre’s sake."]},{"type":"verse","number":12,"content":["One of themselves, a prophet of their own, said,",{"text":"Cretans are always liars, evil beasts, idle gluttons.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":13,"content":["This testimony is true. For which cause reprove them sharply, that they may be sound in the faith,"]},{"type":"verse","number":14,"content":["not giving heed to Jewish fables, and commandments of men who turn away from the truth."]},{"type":"verse","number":15,"content":["To the pure all things are pure: but to them that are defiled and unbelieving nothing is pure; but both their mind and their conscience are defiled."]},{"type":"verse","number":16,"content":["They profess that they know God; but by their works they deny him, being abominable, and disobedient, and unto every good work reprobate."]}],"footnotes":[]}},{"numberOfVerses":15,"chapter":{"number":2,"content":[{"type":"verse","number":1,"content":["But speak thou the things which befit the sound doctrine:"]},{"type":"verse","number":2,"content":["that aged men be temperate, grave, sober-minded, sound in faith, in love, in patience:"]},{"type":"verse","number":3,"content":["that aged women likewise be reverent in demeanor, not slanderers nor enslaved to much wine, teachers of that which is good;"]},{"type":"verse","number":4,"content":["that they may train the young women to love their husbands, to love their children,"]},{"type":"verse","number":5,"content":["to be sober-minded, chaste, workers at home, kind, being in subjection to their own husbands, that the word of God be not blasphemed:"]},{"type":"verse","number":6,"content":["the younger men likewise exhort to be sober-minded:"]},{"type":"verse","number":7,"content":["in all things showing thyself an ensample of good works; in thy doctrine showing uncorruptness, gravity,"]},{"type":"verse","number":8,"content":["sound speech, that cannot be condemned; that he that is of the contrary part may be ashamed, having no evil thing to say of us."]},{"type":"verse","number":9,"content":["Exhort servants to be in subjection to their own masters, and to be well-pleasing to them in all things; not gainsaying;"]},{"type":"verse","number":10,"content":["not purloining, but showing all good fidelity; that they may adorn the doctrine of God our Saviour in all things."]},{"type":"verse","number":11,"content":["For the grace of God hath appeared, bringing salvation to all men,"]},{"type":"verse","number":12,"content":["instructing us, to the intent that, denying ungodliness and worldly lusts, we should live soberly and righteously and godly in this present world;"]},{"type":"verse","number":13,"content":["looking for the blessed hope and appearing of the glory of the great God and our Saviour Jesus Christ;"]},{"type":"verse","number":14,"content":["who gave himself for us, that he might redeem us from all iniquity, and purify unto himself a people for his own possession, zealous of good works."]},{"type":"verse","number":15,"content":["These things speak and exhort and reprove with all authority. Let no man despise thee."]},{"type":"line_break"}],"footnotes":[]}},{"numberOfVerses":15,"chapter":{"number":3,"content":[{"type":"verse","number":1,"content":["Put them in mind to be in subjection to rulers, to authorities, to be obedient, to be ready unto every good work,"]},{"type":"verse","number":2,"content":["to speak evil of no man, not to be contentious, to be gentle, showing all meekness toward all men."]},{"type":"verse","number":3,"content":["For we also once were foolish, disobedient, deceived, serving divers lusts and pleasures, living in malice and envy, hateful, hating one another."]},{"type":"verse","number":4,"content":["But when the kindness of God our Saviour, and his love toward man, appeared,"]},{"type":"verse","number":5,"content":["not by works done in righteousness, which we did ourselves, but according to his mercy he saved us, through the washing of regeneration and renewing of the Holy Spirit,"]},{"type":"verse","number":6,"content":["which he poured out upon us richly, through Jesus Christ our Saviour;"]},{"type":"verse","number":7,"content":["that, being justified by his grace, we might be made heirs according to the hope of eternal life."]},{"type":"verse","number":8,"content":["Faithful is the saying, and concerning these things I desire that thou affirm confidently, to the end that they who have believed God may be careful to maintain good works. These things are good and profitable unto men:"]},{"type":"verse","number":9,"content":["but shun foolish questionings, and genealogies, and strifes, and fightings about the law; for they are unprofitable and vain."]},{"type":"verse","number":10,"content":["A factious man after a first and second admonition refuse;"]},{"type":"verse","number":11,"content":["knowing that such a one is perverted, and sinneth, being self-condemned."]},{"type":"verse","number":12,"content":["When I shall send Artemas unto thee, or Tychicus, give diligence to come unto me to Nicopolis: for there I have determined to winter."]},{"type":"verse","number":13,"content":["Set forward Zenas the lawyer and Apollos on their journey diligently, that nothing be wanting unto them."]},{"type":"verse","number":14,"content":["And let our people also learn to maintain good works for necessary uses, that they be not unfruitful."]},{"type":"verse","number":15,"content":["All that are with me salute thee. Salute them that love us in faith. Grace be with you all."]}],"footnotes":[]}}]}
